# ============================================================================
#  DVAD .gitignore
#
#  Rule of thumb: anything DOWNLOADED, EXTRACTED, or GENERATED at provision
#  time never belongs in git.
#
#  Large payloads are cached HOST-SIDE on purpose. Guests write to
#  C:\vagrant\... which is the Vagrant synced folder, i.e. this repo on the
#  host. That way a failed provision or a `vagrant destroy` never forces a
#  re-download. See cache/README.md.
#
#  History note: ~3 GB of installer payload was committed before these rules
#  existed. Keep the extension catch-alls below broad, and force-include
#  individual files with `!` only when a fresh clone genuinely needs them.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host-side download cache (contents ignored, the README that explains it is not)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache/*
!cache/README.md

# Legacy cache paths still used by the current provisioners. Everything inside
# is downloaded or extracted at run time; only the checked-in config survives.
provisioners/services/SCCM/MECM_Setup/*
!provisioners/services/SCCM/MECM_Setup/ConfigMgrAutoSave.ini
provisioners/services/SCCM/SQL-offline/
provisioners/services/SCCM/ADK/
**/Media/
**/Prereqs/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installer payloads and binaries
# Broad by design: a new .msi/.exe must be opted IN, never leak in by default.
# (This is the gap that let LAPS.x64.msi and msodbcsql.msi get committed.)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.iso
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.vdi
*.vmdk
*.box
*.wim
*.swm
*.msi
*.msp
*.msu
*.cab
*.exe
*.dll

# No force-includes. Every Microsoft/Sysinternals redistributable is staged at
# run time instead of being committed - see inventory/lab-deps.json, and run
# `lab.ps1 deps` to fetch the set your profile needs. This keeps the clone
# small and stops the repo redistributing binaries it has no licence to ship.
provisioners/services/SCCM/sxs/
provisioners/services/SCCM/extendSchema/
provisioners/domain/LAPS/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored attacker tooling + personal notes (fetched / kept out-of-band).
# Whole trees, so repo-wide globs are unnecessary and cannot hide a real file.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
autolab/
AutoLab/
vulns/
provisioners/vulns/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vagrant / runtime output
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vagrant/
junk/
*.log
*.evtx
setup.log

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only tooling (kept on disk, not shipped)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
verify-lab-acl.ps1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / assistant metadata
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.user
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
